# Explicit preferred funder group names

## Problem

The component identity is the minimum surviving UUID, whereas its display name is currently that identity's recorded name. These are separate concerns. A BBC component may have an unrelated alias-connected representative; neither changing that representative nor rewriting its source name is acceptable. Reviewed labels belong to the grouping projection, with policy ownership remaining in `domain/models/funder_grouping.rs` and `funder_families.v1.json`.

## Usage (caller's view)

```rust
// Existing ingestion and refresh call sites remain unchanged.
let groups = build_funder_groups(&funders)?;
// outbound projects memberships, evidence, and groups.preferred_names in one transaction.

db.refresh_funder_groups().await?;
let matches = db.get_funders_by_text_search_score(&request("BBC", 10, 1.0)).await?;
// Same minimum UUID; display "BBC", including when no recorded funder is exactly BBC.
let details = db.funder_funding(member_id).await?;
// Existing requested-ID contract stays; profile.name is BBC; recorded aliases/evidence unchanged.
```

## Shape

Use a sparse, pipeline-owned `exposed.funder_group_names` table with one row per component having an unambiguous reviewed preferred name. Ordinary components continue using their representative's current recorded name. This avoids materializing a redundant fallback name for every group. The domain builder remains the sole policy owner; SQL readers only select persisted labels.

Types inside `domain/models/funder_grouping.rs`:

